2. Representations and Warranties

The Borrower and the Guarantor jointly and severally represent and warrant to the Lender as follows:

2.1. Existence and Authority

The Borrower and the Guarantor are duly organized, validly existing, and in good standing under the laws of the jurisdictions in which they are incorporated, and have the power and authority to enter into and perform their obligations under this agreement.

2.2. Binding Obligation

This agreement has been duly executed and delivered by the Borrower and the Guarantor and constitutes a legal, valid, and binding obligation of each of them, enforceable against them in accordance with its terms, except as enforceability may be limited by bankruptcy, insolvency, or other laws of general applicability.

2.3. Authorization

The execution, delivery, and performance of this agreement by the Borrower and the Guarantor have been duly authorized by all necessary action on their part.

2.4. Loan Repayment

The Borrower has the power, authority, and financial resources to pay the Loan and all amounts due under this agreement when due.

2.5. Guaranty

The Guarantor has the power, authority, and financial resources to fulfill its obligations under this agreement and any guarantees it provides.

2.6. No Conflicts

The execution, delivery, and performance of this agreement by the Borrower and the Guarantor do not conflict with, result in a breach of, or constitute a default under, any agreement, instrument, or other obligation to which either of them is a party or by which they or any of their properties are bound.

2.7. Financial Statements

The Borrower's and the Guarantor's financial statements, as of the date of this agreement, accurately reflect their respective financial conditions, and they have complied in all material respects with all applicable accounting requirements and rules.

2.8. No Litigation

There are no pending or threatened legal proceedings or governmental investigations to which the Borrower or the Guarantor are a party or of which they are aware that may materially affect the financial condition, business, or properties of the Borrower or the Guarantor.

2.9. Compliance with Laws

The Borrower and the Guarantor have complied, and will continue to comply, with all applicable laws, rules, and regulations in the performance of their obligations under this agreement.

2.10. No Conflicting Agreements

The execution, delivery, and performance of this agreement by the Borrower and the Guarantor do not conflict with, result in a breach of, or constitute a default under, any other agreement to which the Borrower or the Guarantor is a party.

The Lender represents and warrants to the Borrower and the Guarantor that it has the power, authority, and financial resources to enter into and perform its obligations under this agreement.

The foregoing representations, warranties, and covenants are made as of the date of this agreement and shall survive the execution and delivery hereof. Each Party acknowledges and agrees that it has relied upon the representations, warranties, and covenants of the other Parties in entering into this agreement.

3. Covenants

TEXT:
3. Covenants

3.1. Use of Loan Proceeds
The Borrower shall use the Loan Proceeds solely for the purpose of funding its research and development projects. The Borrower shall maintain accurate records of the use of the Loan Proceeds and shall provide the Lender with regular updates on the progress of the projects.

3.2. Cross-Default
In the event of a default by the Borrower under any other agreement, the Loan shall automatically accelerate, and the entire outstanding balance shall become immediately due and payable.

3.3. Financial Covenants
The Borrower shall maintain a current ratio of not less than 1.5:1 and a debt-to-equity ratio of not more than 3:1 at all times during the Loan Term. The Borrower shall provide the Lender with monthly financial statements, certified by an independent auditor, to confirm compliance with these financial covenants.

3.4. Restrictions on Payments
The Borrower shall not, without the prior written consent of the Lender, make any payments of dividends, bonuses, or other distributions to its shareholders or directors, or repay any indebtedness, during the Loan Term, except for payments required by law or for ordinary course of business trade payables.

3.5. Mergers and Acquisitions
The Borrower shall not, without the prior written consent of the Lender, enter into any merger, consolidation, sale of assets, or other transaction that would result in a change of control of the Borrower, or any other transaction that would materially affect the Borrower's financial condition or business.

3.6. Notices
The Borrower shall promptly notify the Lender of any material adverse change in its financial condition, business, or properties, or any event that may result in a default under this agreement.

3.7. Information and Access
The Borrower shall provide the Lender with such information and access to its books, records, and facilities as the Lender may reasonably request to enable the Lender to monitor the Borrower's compliance with its obligations under this agreement.

3.8. Amendments
No amendment or modification of this agreement shall be binding unless in writing and signed by both Parties.

3.9. Survival
The covenants in this Section shall survive the termination or expiration of this agreement.

3.10. Waiver
The waiver by the Lender of any breach of a covenant by the Borrower shall not operate as a waiver of any subsequent breach of the same or any other covenant.

3.11. Entire Agreement
This Section contains the entire agreement between the Parties regarding the covenants and shall supersede any prior understandings or agreements, whether written or oral, relating to the subject matter hereof.

3.12. Counterparts
This Section may be executed in counterparts, each of which shall be deemed an original, but all of which together shall constitute one and the same instrument.

3.13. Governing Law
This Section shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of England and Wales.

3.14. Disputes
Any disputes arising out of or in connection with this Section shall be resolved by arbitration in accordance with the rules of the London Court of International Arbitration. The seat of the arbitration shall be London, England. The language of the arbitration shall be English.

3.15. Severability
If any provision of this Section is held to be invalid, illegal, or unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect.

3.16. Time of the Essence
Time is of the essence in the performance of the Borrower's obligations under this Section.

3.17. Further Assurances
Each Party shall execute and deliver such further documents and do such further acts as may be reasonably necessary to carry out the purposes and intent of this Section.

3.18. Headings
The headings in this Section are for convenience only and shall not affect the interpretation of this Section.

