6. Default and Remedies

6. Default and Remedies

6.1. Default
A default under this Agreement shall occur if:

6.1.1. The Borrower fails to make any payment when due;
6.1.2. The Borrower breaches any covenant or representation contained in this Agreement;
6.1.3. The Borrower fails to maintain the financial covenants as set forth in Section 3;
6.1.4. The Borrower becomes insolvent, files for bankruptcy, or makes an assignment for the benefit of creditors;
6.1.5. The Borrower takes any action that would reasonably be expected to materially and adversely affect the value of the Loan or the Lender's ability to collect on the Loan.

6.2. Remedies
Upon the occurrence of a default, the Lender shall have the right to:

6.2.1. Accelerate the Loan, including all accrued and unpaid interest and fees, and demand immediate payment in full;
6.2.2. Foreclose on the security interest granted by the Borrower pursuant to Section 4.6;
6.2.3. Exercise any other rights and remedies available to the Lender under applicable law, including, but not limited to, seeking specific performance, injunctive relief, or damages.

6.3. Cure
The Borrower shall have the right to cure any default within [INSERT CURE PERIOD], provided that the Borrower pays all amounts due and complies with all other conditions required by the Lender to cure the default. If the Borrower cures the default, the Lender's rights and remedies under this Section shall terminate.

6.4. Waiver
The failure of the Lender to exercise any right or remedy under this Section shall not constitute a waiver of such right or remedy, and the Lender shall have the right to exercise such right or remedy at any time.

6.5. No Waiver
The failure of the Lender to require performance by the Borrower of any provision of this Agreement shall not affect the validity of the provision or any other provision of this Agreement, nor shall it be construed as a waiver of any subsequent breach of such provision or any other provision of this Agreement.

